{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1920,
 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "The Barnacle gang's boat crossed an ocean, then sank in a river.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.199
  },
  {
   "text": "It was carrying two tons of stolen gold bars, hidden under frozen fish.",
   "s": 3.399,
   "e": 7.223
  },
  {
   "text": "At sea, Captain Gill loaded it right to the brim. \"Every inch is money!\"",
   "s": 7.423,
   "e": 10.967
  },
  {
   "text": "Sir Whiskers, the ship's cat, wanted only one thing in life: dry paws.",
   "s": 11.087,
   "e": 14.444
  },
  {
   "text": "The boat sat so low that waves licked the deck. Still, it floated.",
   "s": 14.644,
   "e": 18.024
  },
  {
   "text": "The plan was to sneak up the Mudd River to their hideout, an old pickle factory.",
   "s": 18.224,
   "e": 22.199
  },
  {
   "text": "But the moment it left the salty sea, the boat started sinking. Slowly, like it had changed its mind.",
   "s": 22.399,
   "e": 27.537
  },
  {
   "text": "First the deck went under. Then the fish. Then the captain's hat.",
   "s": 27.737,
   "e": 30.064
  },
  {
   "text": "So Gill threw the fish overboard. \"Every inch is money!\" The fish thawed and swam home.",
   "s": 30.264,
   "e": 34.133
  },
  {
   "text": "It kept sinking anyway, and the police waited on the riverbank with lemonade.",
   "s": 34.333,
   "e": 38.079
  },
  {
   "text": "So how can a boat float at sea and sink in a river?",
   "s": 38.279,
   "e": 40.406
  },
  {
   "text": "Sea water is full of salt, which makes it heavier. Heavier water pushes up harder.",
   "s": 40.706,
   "e": 44.571
  },
  {
   "text": "River water is lighter, so the same boat sinks deeper. Load it to the brim at sea, and the river finishes the job.",
   "s": 44.971,
   "e": 50.777
  },
  {
   "text": "That's why big ships wear a load line: a sea mark, and a higher river mark.",
   "s": 50.977,
   "e": 54.449
  },
  {
   "text": "The gold went back to the bank. \"Every inch is money,\" said Gill, from a very small cell.",
   "s": 54.649,
   "e": 58.973
  },
  {
   "text": "Sir Whiskers rode home, perfectly dry, on a policeman's hat.",
   "s": 59.173,
   "e": 62.17
  }
 ],
